
---
data_dictionary: framingham.txt

description: >
  This dataset contains 1,406 observations from the Framingham Heart Study.
  The data include participants whose cholesterol was measured during
  the first examination. Variables include serum cholesterol, age, sex,
  systolic blood pressure, diastolic blood pressure, and number of
  cigarettes smoked per day. 
copyright: >
  The dataset is attributed to Statistical Methods in Epidemiology
  by H.A. Kahn and C.T. Sempos. It can be accessed through The Data and Story Library.
  It was last accessed by Sudhiksha Kumar on 11/22/2026.

format:
  tab-delimited

varnames:
  first row of data

missing_value_code:
  Blank fields are interpreted as missing values (NA).

size:
  rows: 1406
  columns: 6

vars:
  Cholesterol:
    label: Serum cholesterol level at first examination
    scale: numeric
    unit: not specified in the available dataset documentation

  Age:
    label: Age of participant at first examination
    scale: positive integer
    unit: years

  Sex:
    label: Sex of participant
    value:
      MALE
      FEM

  SBP:
    label: Systolic blood pressure at first examination
    scale: positive integer
    unit: not specified in the available dataset documentation

  DBP:
    label: Diastolic blood pressure at first examination
    scale: positive integer
    unit: not specified in the available dataset documentation

  CIG:
    label: Number of cigarettes smoked per day at first examination
    scale: non-negative integer
    unit: cigarettes per day
